Ritemark Help Menu Policy: keep the product menu focused and fail closed
v1.10.0 RC bug fix:
  - Restores the intentional Support / View License / Advanced menu
  - Applies one allowlist to both native and custom menubars
  - Keeps unknown future VS Code Help contributions hidden by default
  - Keeps commands available through the Command Menu
  - Covers the policy and separator normalization with unit tests
Sprint 133: Getting started joins Support in Help, where 1.x's first page linked to it
Sprint 135: rebased onto VS Code 1.142.0. The main menu's registrations moved upstream to
menubar.contribution.ts; the Help allowlist stays in menubarControl.ts, which now imports MenuRegistry itself.
Upstream added its own menubarControl.test.ts (Open Recent's labels); this patch's suite is appended to it.
Sprint 140 (R10, D7): Help ▸ Send feedback after Support (ritemark.help.sendFeedback, in the allowlist), opening the
extension's feedback sheet through ritemark.feedback.open; off the palette, where the extension's own Send Feedback is.
